{title: Draw Me Nearer}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby / William H. Doane}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I am [G]Thine, O Lord, I have [C]heard Thy [G]voice
And it [D7]told Thy love to [G]me
But I [G]long to rise in the [C]arms of [G]faith
And be [D7]closer drawn to [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Draw me nearer, nearer, [C]blessed [G]Lord
To the [D7]cross where Thou hast [G]died
[G]Draw me nearer, nearer, [C]nearer, [G]blessed Lord
To Thy [D7]precious, bleeding [G]side
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Con[G]secrate me now to Thy [C]service, [G]Lord
By the [D7]power of grace di[G]vine
Let my [G]soul look up with a [C]steadfast [G]hope
And my [D7]will be lost in [G]Thine
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
O the [G]pure delight of a [C]single [G]hour
That be[D7]fore Thy throne I [G]spend
When I [G]kneel in prayer, and with [C]Thee, my [G]God
I com[D7]mune as friend with [G]friend
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
There are [G]depths of love that I [C]cannot [G]know
Till I [D7]cross the narrow [G]sea
There are [G]heights of joy that I [C]may not [G]reach
Till I [D7]rest in peace with [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
